  "worked_solution": "The  $2\\times 2$ matrix represents the coefficients of $x$ and $y,$ while the $2\\times 1$ column vector on the right-hand side represents the constants of the equations. So, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x-5y=10 \\\\ x+0y=-7\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying both equations in the system, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x-5y=10 \\\\ x=-7\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
